 "story": [
  "**Faults are rare:** 456 of 4,205 recordings (10.8 %) are abnormal, so accuracy alone is misleading. The model is judged on precision, recall, F1 and PR-AUC for the abnormal class.",
  "**A faulty pump keeps its hum but adds hiss:** below 300 Hz the classes are within 0.4 dB; from 300 Hz to 8 kHz abnormal clips are about **2 dB louder**, so the share of energy below 500 Hz falls from 65 % to 56 %.",
  "**Louder and noisier, but only a little:** abnormal clips are slightly louder and noisier, yet no single feature separates the classes well (best single-feature ROC-AUC **0.71**).",
  "**Every pump has its own normal:** pump id_04's healthy sound is noisier than other pumps' faulty sound, so fixed rules fail. The CNN learns patterns across 64 frequency bands and 10 s of time instead."
 ],
